></path><g transform="matrix(-0.60011 -0.79993 0.79993 -0.60011 6.73 8.97)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.98 0 C 3.51 0.28 1.11 1.11 -0.55 2.08 L -0.55 -2.08 C 1.11 -1.11 3.51 -0.28 4.98 0"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 91.17 27.07 L 77.59 8.97"></path><g transform="matrix(-0.60011 -0.79993 0.79993 -0.60011 77.59 8.97)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.98 0 C 3.51 0.28 1.11 1.11 -0.55 2.08 L -0.55 -2.08 C 1.11 -1.11 3.51 -0.28 4.98 0"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 162.04 27.07 L 148.46 8.97"></path><g transform="matrix(-0.60011 -0.79993 0.79993 -0.60011 148.46 8.97)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.98 0 C 3.51 0.28 1.11 1.11 -0.55 2.08 L -0.55 -2.08 C 1.11 -1.11 3.51 -0.28 4.98 0"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 232.9 27.07 L 219.32 8.97"></path><g transform="matrix(-0.60011 -0.79991 0.79991 -0.60011 219.32 8.97)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.98 0 C 3.51 0.28 1.11 1.11 -0.55 2.08 L -0.55 -2.08 C 1.11 -1.11 3.51 -0.28 4.98 0"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 303.77 27.07 L 290.19 8.97"></path><g transform="matrix(-0.60011 -0.79991 0.79991 -0.60011 290.19 8.97)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.98 0 C 3.51 0.28 1.11 1.11 -0.55 2.08 L -0.55 -2.08 C 1.11 -1.11 3.51 -0.28 4.98 0"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 374.64 27.07 L 361.06 8.97"></path><g transform="matrix(-0.60011 -0.79993 0.79993 -0.60011 361.06 8.97)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 4.98 0 C 3.51 0.28 1.11 1.11 -0.55 2.08 L -0.55 -2.08 C 1.11 -1.11 3.51 -0.28 4.98 0"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>The only possible structure of any <math id="S4.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent colouring of <math id="S4.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[Z_{0}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[Z_{0}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Vertices coloured <math id="S4.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> are in blue, and vertices coloured <math id="S4.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> in orange. As indicated by the twisting arrows, the acyclic ordering of each <math id="S4.F4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.F4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\geqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\geqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>, goes from right to left.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS2.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us thus fix <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leqslant j\leqslant\ell+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leqslant j\leqslant\ell+1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}\subseteq Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}\subseteq Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{0,\ell+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{0,\ell+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> then, in every <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent colouring, all vertices in <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> must be coloured <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}\subseteq N^{+}(s)\cup N^{-}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}\subseteq N^{+}(s)\cup N^{-}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Henceforth, assume that <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leqslant j\leqslant\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leqslant j\leqslant\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. By Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim3" title="Claim 0.3. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.3</span></a><a href="#S4.I1.i2" title="Item (ii) ‣ Claim 0.3. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(ii)</span></a> and <a href="#S4.I1.i3" title="Item (iii) ‣ Claim 0.3. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(iii)</span></a>, <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}\subseteq N^{+}(v_{j})\cap N^{-}(v_{j-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}\subseteq N^{+}(v_{j})\cap N^{-}(v_{j-1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p26.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is acyclic.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p27" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p27.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p27.1.1" class="ltx_text">If <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(v_{j-1})=\gamma(v_{j})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(v_{j-1})=\gamma(v_{j})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then in every <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent colouring extending <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, every vertex <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> must be coloured <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, for otherwise <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{j-1},v_{j},x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{j-1},v_{j},x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a monochromatic directed triangle in <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[Z_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[Z_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly, if <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(v_{j-1})=\gamma(v_{j})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(v_{j-1})=\gamma(v_{j})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, there is only one possible extension of <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p27.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p28" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p28.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p28.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume finally that <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1=\gamma(v_{j-1})\neq\gamma(v_{j})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1=\gamma(v_{j-1})\neq\gamma(v_{j})=2</annotation></semantics></math>, the other remaining case being symmetric. Let <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1},\dots,x_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1},\dots,x_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> be the acyclic ordering of <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[X_{j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[X_{j}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=|X_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=|X_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math>. In every <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent extension <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, and for every <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leqslant a&lt;b\leqslant r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⩽</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leqslant a&lt;b\leqslant r</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(x_{a})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(x_{a})=1</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta(x_{b})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta(x_{b})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, for otherwise <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(v_{j-1},v_{j},x_{a},x_{b})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(v_{j-1},v_{j},x_{a},x_{b})</annotation></semantics></math> is an alternating directed cycle.
Therefore, <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by the index <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in[0,r]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in[0,r]</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x_{b})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x_{b})=1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&gt;a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&gt;a</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi(x_{b})=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi(x_{b})=2</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\leqslant a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\leqslant a</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows that at most <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r+1\leqslant n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r+1\leqslant n+1</annotation></semantics></math> colourings of <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[X_{j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[X_{j}]</annotation></semantics></math> may extend <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and the claim follows.
  <math id="S4.SS2.p28.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lozenge" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">◊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lozenge</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p29" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p29.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p29.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now compute, for every <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[k]</annotation></semantics></math>, the set <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent colourings of <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[Z_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[Z_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be done in polynomial time by the second part of Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim5" title="Claim 0.5. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.5</span></a>.
By Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim4" title="Claim 0.4. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.4</span></a>, we know that <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a nice pair if and only if there exists a colouring <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> such that, for every <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[0,k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[0,k]</annotation></semantics></math>, the restriction of <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="S4.SS2.p29.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p30" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p30.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p30.1.1" class="ltx_text">For every <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[0,k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[0,k]</annotation></semantics></math> and colouring <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[Z_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[Z_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\leqslant i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\leqslant i)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS2.p30.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">-coherent</span> if there exists an extension <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[\bigcup_{j=0}^{i}Z_{j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[\bigcup_{j=0}^{i}Z_{j}]</annotation></semantics></math> whose restriction to <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> belongs to <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in[0,i]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in[0,i]</annotation></semantics></math>. We further denote by <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\leqslant i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\leqslant i)</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent colourings of <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[Z_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[Z_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math>. To decide whether <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a nice pair, it only remains to decide whether <math id="S4.SS2.p30.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{k}^{\star}\neq\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{k}^{\star}\neq\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p31" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p31.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p31.1.1" class="ltx_text">Observe that, by definition, <math id="S4.SS2.p31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{0}^{\star}=\mathcal{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{0}^{\star}=\mathcal{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can recursively build <math id="S4.SS2.p31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS2.p31.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> as follows.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_claim">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Claim 0.6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every <math id="Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[1,k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[1,k]</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}=\{\varphi\in\mathcal{C}_{i}\mid\mbox{there exists }\psi\in\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}\mbox{ such that }\varphi(u)=\psi(u)\text{ for all }u\in Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">there exists </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> such that </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic"> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}=\{\varphi\in\mathcal{C}_{i}\mid\mbox{there exists }\psi\in\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}\mbox{ such that }\varphi(u)=\psi(u)\text{ for all }u\in Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p32" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p32.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p32.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of claim</span>. Let first <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> be any colouring in <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> be its extension to <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[\bigcup_{j=0}^{i}Z_{j}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[\bigcup_{j=0}^{i}Z_{j}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly the restriction of <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\in\mathcal{C}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\in\mathcal{C}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the restriction <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\leqslant i-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\leqslant i-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent, as witnessed by the restriction of <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. This shows</p>
<table id="S4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}\subseteq\{\varphi\in\mathcal{C}_{i}\mid\mbox{there exists }\psi\in\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}\mbox{ such that }\varphi(u)=\psi(u)\text{ for all }u\in Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>there exists </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> such that </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}\subseteq\{\varphi\in\mathcal{C}_{i}\mid\mbox{there exists }\psi\in\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}\mbox{ such that }\varphi(u)=\psi(u)\text{ for all }u\in Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p32.2" class="ltx_p">For the opposite direction, let <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> be any <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent colouring of <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[Z_{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[Z_{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> such that there exists <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi\in\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi\in\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> agreeing with <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\leqslant i-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\leqslant i-1)</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent, there exists an extension <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> whose restriction to any set <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leqslant i-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leqslant i-1</annotation></semantics></math>, is <math id="S4.SS2.p32.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p33" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p33.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p33.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> be the colouring of <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="T[\bigcup_{j=0}^{i}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[\bigcup_{j=0}^{i}]</annotation></semantics></math> equal to <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and to <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>. This is possible because <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\star}(u)=\psi(u)=\varphi(u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\star}(u)=\psi(u)=\varphi(u)</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and because</span></p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}\cap\Big(\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}\Big)=Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}\cap\Big(\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}\Big)=Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p33.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p33.2.1" class="ltx_text">To see that (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) holds, we use the definition of the sets <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>s and the fact that <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(P),X_{0},\dots,X_{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(P),X_{0},\dots,X_{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math> are pairwise disjoint (by Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim3" title="Claim 0.3. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.3</span></a><a href="#S4.I1.i4" title="Item (iv) ‣ Claim 0.3. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">(iv)</span></a>). Using these facts, we conclude that:</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}\cap Z_{i-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\subseteq Z_{i}\cap\Big(\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\subseteq Z_{i}\cap\Big(\bigcup_{j=0}^{i-1}Z_{j}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big(\{v_{i-1},\dots,v_{i+6}\}\cup\bigcup_{j=i}^{i+6}X_{j}\Big)\cap\Big(\{v_{0},\dots,v_{i+5}\}\cup\bigcup_{j=0}^{i+5}X_{j}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big(\{v_{i-1},\dots,v_{i+6}\}\cup\bigcup_{j=i}^{i+6}X_{j}\Big)\cap\Big(\{v_{0},\dots,v_{i+5}\}\cup\bigcup_{j=0}^{i+5}X_{j}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
