<p id="S4.SS2.p33.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p33.3.1" class="ltx_text">implying (<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
It follows by construction that the restriction of <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>φ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> to any set <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\leqslant i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\leqslant i</annotation></semantics></math>, is <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent, and thus <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi\in\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi\in\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>. The claim follows.
  <math id="S4.SS2.p33.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lozenge" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">◊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lozenge</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p34" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p34.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p34.1.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim6" title="Claim 0.6. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.6</span></a> that, given <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can build <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in polynomial time (since both <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i-1}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> have size at most <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n^{6})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{6})</annotation></semantics></math> by Claim <a href="#Thmtheorem0.Thmclaim5" title="Claim 0.5. ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ 4.2 A polynomial-time algorithm for Acyclic 2-Dicolouring on tournaments ‣ 4 Complexity ‣ Acyclic dichromatic number of oriented graphs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.5</span></a>). After <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leqslant n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leqslant n</annotation></semantics></math> steps, in particular, we know whether <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{k}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{k}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is empty, and thus whether <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a nice pair.
Moreover, if <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a nice pair, an <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,t)</annotation></semantics></math>-colouring <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> can be obtained with a simple backtracking, starting from any colouring of <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[Z_{k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[Z_{k}]</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{k}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{k}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> and, for <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=k-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=k-1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, extending it to <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> by choosing any colouring in <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{i}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> equal to <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS2.p34.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
