<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(\ell/2,0)=\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}\ell(\ell-2)}&lt;\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}\ell^{2}-2\ell}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(\ell/2,0)=\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}\ell(\ell-2)}&lt;\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}\ell^{2}-2\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.5.1" class="ltx_text">and that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\left(\frac{\ell-3}{2},1\right)&lt;\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}(\ell^{2}-8\ell+15)}&lt;\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}\ell^{2}-2\ell}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\left(\frac{\ell-3}{2},1\right)&lt;\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}(\ell^{2}-8\ell+15)}&lt;\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}\ell^{2}-2\ell},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.6.1" class="ltx_text">where in the last inequality we used that <math id="S5.p19.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> (and thus <math id="S5.p19.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p19.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>) is large enough, so <math id="S5.p19.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell&gt;15/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell&gt;15/8</annotation></semantics></math>.
In both cases, we conclude that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\Big((X_{1},\dots,X_{t})\mbox{ is an acyclic partition}\Big)&lt;\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}\ell^{2}-2\ell}=2^{-\frac{1}{\beta}\ell^{2}+16\beta\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is an acyclic partition</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\Big((X_{1},\dots,X_{t})\mbox{ is an acyclic partition}\Big)&lt;\left(\frac{7}{8}\right)^{\frac{1}{8}\ell^{2}-2\ell}=2^{-\frac{1}{\beta}\ell^{2}+16\beta\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.7.1" class="ltx_text">For a fixed set of vertices <math id="S5.p19.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="S5.p19.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, there are at most <math id="S5.p19.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\ell}=2^{\ell\log(\ell)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\ell}=2^{\ell\log(\ell)}</annotation></semantics></math> partitions of <math id="S5.p19.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>. It thus follows from the union bound that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(X\mbox{ is partitionable})&lt;2^{-\frac{1}{\beta}\ell^{2}+\ell\log(\ell)+16\beta\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is partitionable</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(X\mbox{ is partitionable})&lt;2^{-\frac{1}{\beta}\ell^{2}+\ell\log(\ell)+16\beta\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.8.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, there exist exactly <math id="S5.p19.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{n}{\ell}&lt;n^{\ell}=2^{\ell\log(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{n}{\ell}&lt;n^{\ell}=2^{\ell\log(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> sets of vertices of size <math id="S5.p19.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>. By the union bound again, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\Big(\exists X\subseteq V(T),|X|=\ell,\text{ $X$ is partitionable}\Big)&lt;2^{\ell\log(n)-\frac{1}{\beta}\ell^{2}+\ell\log(\ell)+16\beta\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>X</mi><mtext> is partitionable</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\Big(\exists X\subseteq V(T),|X|=\ell,\text{ $X$ is partitionable}\Big)&lt;2^{\ell\log(n)-\frac{1}{\beta}\ell^{2}+\ell\log(\ell)+16\beta\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.9.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="S5.p19.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leqslant\ell\leqslant k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leqslant\ell\leqslant k+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ell\log(n)-\frac{1}{\beta}\ell^{2}+\ell\log(\ell)+16\beta\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ell\log(n)-\frac{1}{\beta}\ell^{2}+\ell\log(\ell)+16\beta\ell</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant k\log(n)-\frac{1}{\beta}k^{2}+k\log(k)+O(\log n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant k\log(n)-\frac{1}{\beta}k^{2}+k\log(k)+O(\log n)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S5.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant(1-\beta)\log(n)\log\log(n)+O(\log(n))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant(1-\beta)\log(n)\log\log(n)+O(\log(n))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.10.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S5.p19.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and because <math id="S5.p19.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough, it follows that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\Big(\exists X\subseteq V(T),|X|=\ell,\text{ $X$ is partitionable}\Big)&lt;\frac{1}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext> </mtext><mi>X</mi><mtext> is partitionable</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\Big(\exists X\subseteq V(T),|X|=\ell,\text{ $X$ is partitionable}\Big)&lt;\frac{1}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.p19.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p19.11.1" class="ltx_text">It is straightforward to check that the exact same argument applied with <math id="S5.p19.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell+1</annotation></semantics></math> instead of <math id="S5.p19.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> holds, hence implying that</span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
